    14	2. From this skill directory, run the command below. Replace URLs and dates for a new manager request. The source order is interchangeable; roles are identified from headers. Network access must be allowed by the operator's environment.
    15	3. Confirm exit status 0 and `DRAFT READY`. Review the three printed `SOURCE` metadata records, then open `../deliverables/report.md`. Check the five signed daily figures, budget and snapshot evidence, and the full unresolved queue. Hand the draft to the Operations Owner for review; do not execute financial decisions or contact source owners automatically.
    16	4. On a nonzero exit, use stderr to identify the failed access or evidence check. Required CSVs are removed and the report is marked unavailable. Request clarification from Operations for ledger issues or Finance for budget/revenue issues. Rerun the same full command after resolution; every rerun freshly reads all three sources.
    17	
    18	## One end-to-end command
    19	
    20	Runtime: Python 3.10+ on Linux, macOS or WSL, with HTTPS access to the supplied view-only Sheets and a writable output directory. Uses only the standard library (`urllib`, `csv`, `decimal`, `fcntl` and related modules). No install step, API key, connector login or third-party runtime dependency. Tested on Python 3.14.4; a live run of the disclosed sources took approximately 2.7 seconds. Network latency varies; each request has a 30-second timeout and a 10 MB input limit.
